    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) and **Yordan Alvarez** (81.16) anchoring our lineup as the premier plays. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an ideal confluence of variables: a favorable matchup against Matthews, a dynamic platoon advantage (+14%), and a slow opposing delivery that screams stolen base potential. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start despite the ballpark park adjustment; his elite xwOBA of 0.477 and strong SP matchup against Young make him our most dangerous offensive threat. **Colt Keith** (68.51) and **Junior Caminero** (68.25) also provide high-floor production, with both hitters leveraging significant platoon edges and favorable lineup positioning to climb near the 70-point threshold.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Lars Nootbaar** (49.51), who fell just shy of cracking the starting nine. While **Lars Nootbaar** enjoys a solid SP matchup against Rodriguez, his efficiency was capped by a lower projected batting order spot and a negative dynamic platoon adjustment, which pushed him behind **Carson Benge** (54.69) for the final outfield slot. Managers should monitor **Pete Crow-Armstrong** closely, as the \"Wind In\" warning provides a slight risk to his power upside, though his speed-first profile mitigates the overall impact on his category contribution. Elsewhere, **Trea Turner** faces a challenge against McLean; while his elite speed is essential for our SB-heavy strategy, his score (57.68) is tempered by the opposing pitcher's high skill level, requiring him to rely on his leadoff role to manufacture value.",
